//! The `break-inside` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets how
//! page, column, or region breaks should behave inside a generated box. If there is no generated
//! box, the property is ignored.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | avoid | avoid-page | avoid-column | avoid-region
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-break-4/#propdef-break-inside
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/break-inside
